e03606963a4fc1","cmd-a07b902bef504034","cmd-109273f9b69b44fa","cmd-19028073a9094628","cmd-7832614594684fc8","cmd-606b197a2a354006","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider restart protocol also captured a healthy task-service baseline with boot ID b4e86aa0-4c66-496b-b950-2972794ccf9d, an acknowledged reboot, a new boot ID c7a1bd2b-e5ad-4cca-8fcc-12885866339d, and recovery of service state, identical content, loopback access, and external-address isolation. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The external-address probes originated on node1 rather than a separate host, although the exclusive 127.0.0.1 socket binding strongly corroborates the isolation result (cmd-109273f9b69b44fa, cmd-606b197a2a354006).","The node-wide systemd state was reported as degraded before and after reboot because ssh.service was already failed. Task-service health and recovery were directly demonstrated, but globally healthy systemd state was not; this pre-existing condition is not attributable to the executor (cmd-f98f9bd521f743db, cmd-6fa1a47bca724d6e, global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services, global:after_executor:node1:failed-services)."]}
